  "response_text": "If the thread function did not loop continuously the thread would terminate as soon as the function terminated and would result in a hard fault due to a lack of a return address. When the processor attempts to return to an address that does not exist, a hard fault occurs to protect the system and to stop the processor from going to a random area of memory. The return address would be stored on the link register at the point when print_continuously was first called, and would tell the thread what to do afterwards, because the link register is not updated properly, it would hard fault when print_continuously terminates\\n",
